#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175910 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175736 :question/id #uuid "4dd86f6d-270f-5942-b7cf-df53a0bf4ee4" :question/math-academy-id "e-14361" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0,1)$ and is parallel to the line $y=\\dfrac{2}{3}x + 5$." :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{2}{3}x + 5\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{2}{3}x + 5\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nthat passes through the point $(0,1)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 1 &= \\frac{2}{3}(x - 0) \\\\\ny - 1 &= \\frac{2}{3}x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2}{3}x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4dcbc520-40b5-5c08-ba56-be105c135240" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049716 :topic/math-academy-id 1240 :topic/title "Equations of Lines in Slope-Intercept Form"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050245 :topic/math-academy-id 837 :topic/title "Parallel Lines in the Coordinate Plane"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050635 :topic/math-academy-id 418 :topic/title "Equations of Lines in Point-Slope Form"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481545 :question-generator/id #uuid "efc79b25-de1d-5f31-994e-0a7d81b23c65" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186175910.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "20f45c71-4449-5cf6-9933-4eba8f82dccf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174747}] :question/id #uuid "10c44579-dc85-566b-8520-b63fbd992d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-215701" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4d7c284501bcfffef962