6d-5986-bae3-9f510a8f39a9" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f873e0b53e0dfa21e5b62089544b548f0426b131ab65002e9f724fb8da78dc72.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y = -x + 5$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -x + 5\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -x + 5\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n-1\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope $-1$ that passes through the point $(0,3)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= -1(x - (0)) \\\\\ny &= -x + (3) \\\\\ny &= -x + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1a9f23-4d3f-5b91-8f19-3ccc24a7cb2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e1a9f23-4d3f-5b91-8f19-3ccc24a7cb2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481497} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0cc25a3-5019-559e-be25-ea9080469ddc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481531}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea70257c-2564-520a-b066-c09d7af0e23f" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3c8da343b77f1698c435527613badab50f1645598e8475c3fd2aa1a3d5245427.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y =-\\frac{2}{3}x + 1$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{2}{3}x + 1\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{2}{3}x + 1\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$ that passes through the point $(-6,3)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= -\\frac{2}{3}(x - (-6)) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x - 4 + (3) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e1c90b5-d8ec-56c9-8684-dc5b6ebedb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = -3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481515} {:answer/id #uuid "7e36cc95-946b-533a-a34c-9706206a04a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481517} {:answer/id #uuid "a844402d-d6e7-5ea8-9157-a45d0fdd8e24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481521} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c7515c-8827-5334-9e36-2154adc9efbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = -3x + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481527} {:answer/id #uuid "ee252d66-3d59-526d-aa6d-700c2f5da450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = -3x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0c7515c-8827-5334-9e36-2154adc9efbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = -3x + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481527} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0696c3a-540f-58ff-9616-31cdad0b0106" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481539}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4ec0d10-9ecf-55db-812c-8c2781886239" :question/problem "![](images/db/dbbf49fd68a78969b5b5050f703848a5832bc533e5d2c236389683982901ad9d.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y = -3x + 5$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -3x + 5\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -3x + 5\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n-3\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope $-3$ that passes through the point $(0,3)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= -3(x - (0)) \\\\\ny &= -3x + (3) \\\\\ny &= -3x + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cba75a6-b389-580d-9484-ecd4f0200a12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = -3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481506} {:answer/id #uuid "4f82bade-02b4-5fbf-a007-72dbcc424105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3x + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481511} {:answer/id #uuid "65190d89-49b5-5fda-ab55-6841ced874e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481512} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b4ccdc-e28e-5506-9cd0-294ed2d90537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481528} {:answer/id #uuid "f44e1dc0-ddc5-5eaf-a71d-4d2449aa8967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = -3x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f82bade-02b4-5fbf-a007-72dbcc424105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3x + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481511} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc177dac-11d2-54e1-bf1c-b70a22275365" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481526}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5797ea3-bc2d-51fe-9adc-fde728d4e47d" :question/problem "![](images/95/95f066686cfcee7d1bbb9c451bd6ea007c8bb5433bee6eda06f886d241280180.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y = 3x + 3$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = 3x + 3\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = 3x + 3\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n3\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope $3$ that passes through the point $(0,1)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (1) &= 3(x - (0)) \\\\\ny &= 3x + (1) \\\\\ny &= 3x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d21854e5-c76d-59bc-87eb-08b5c002fa75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d21854e5-c76d-59bc-87eb-08b5c002fa75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481532} :answer-field/id #uuid "7812f2c1-a5b3-503d-a754-6cf928ad7d6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481516}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc76128b-1dbf-5fe8-8ff5-5650472a624c" :question/problem "![](images/e7/e73ff4c357b70c3c740666cab209f33cf08236f9244f044009905a6123cff6b4.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y =-\\frac{3}{2}x$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope $-\\frac{3}{2}$ that passes through the point $(-2,1)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (1) &= -\\frac{3}{2}(x - (-2)) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{3}{2}x - 3 + (1) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{3}{2}x - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line Passing Through a Point"}]}
